---
// Looping background video + scrim for a page's hero/intro band — drop as the
// first two children of a `.hero` or `.band-dark` element (both already have
// the CSS to position/stack these, see _components.scss). WebM first since
// it's ~48% smaller than the H.264 fallback at comparable quality; browsers
// that can't decode WebM skip to the .mp4 source automatically. Hidden below
// the tablet breakpoint and under prefers-reduced-motion (see
// _components.scss) — the parent's own static background-image/color covers
// that case, so there's no separate <img> fallback needed here.
//
// Both files are a forward-then-reverse "boomerang" (~15.9s: the original 8s
// clip followed by itself played backward, minus one frame at each end to avoid
// a held-frame stutter at the two turnarounds) baked into the file itself, so
// the plain `loop` attribute below just repeats that whole boomerang — no JS
// needed to fake reverse playback (browsers don't support negative
// playbackRate on <video>, and manually scrubbing currentTime to simulate it
// stutters badly since video codecs aren't built for cheap backward seeking).
// Re-run the same ffmpeg filter graph (see git history on these two files) if
// the source clip is ever replaced: reverse only needs a straight loop, this
// needs a re-encode.
---

<video
  class="hero-video"
  autoplay
  muted
  loop
  playsinline
  preload="none"
  poster="/assets/hero-video-poster.webp"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <source src="/assets/hero-video-bkg.webm" type="video/webm" />
  <source src="/assets/hero-video-bkg.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
</video>
<div class="hero-video-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
